Hi all,

Since finishing all of the classes in vanilla Nethack I decided to try
a conduct game.  This is really more like it - much more challenging
and fun, in my opinion.

I went with a Monk.  My conducts by the end were:

You were vegetarian.
You never hit with a wielded weapon.
You never genocided any monsters.
You never changed form.
You used no wishes.

Also - No body armor.

Vegetarian wasn't so hard.  In fact Vegan wouldn't be much harder,
especially if you find Ludios before getting hungry and low on food.

No wielded weapon - I ruined a few Monks before this one by
accidentally hitting something with a pickaxe.  This time I was very
cautious.

No genocide - I quit genocide a long time ago.  The game is just more
intresting with L's and h's alive.

Never changed form - I usually don't polymorph anyway.

No wishes - Makes for a much greater challenge.

No body armor - I elected to never wear body armor.

The one thing I did do was polypile, with the single wand of poly I
found.  I think I could have won without poly-piling but, when it came
down to it I just wanted a ring of slow digestion.  I never found a
naturally occuring one until Gehennom.

Stuff I never found:

* Bag of holding.  Made inventory control very interesting.  I had to
trek back to my stash a lot for forgotten spells and holy water.  I
left all gems and coins behind since score didn't matter to me.

* Ring of levigation.  Had to carry different boots around with me.  I
had a scare coming out of the Sanctum when I realized I had no
levitation boots and my Lev spell was forgotten.  Luckily I had a wand
of teleport and got away from the lava.

* Magic Whistle - never found one.  One of my key strategies is usually
Charm Monster / Magic Whistle.

* Scroll of charging - never found one.

As luck would have it, smoky potions were Full Healing.  So I passed up
at least 4 Djinn wishes.  Also found one magic lamp and there were 2
zaps in the castle wand, making 11 wishes I ignored.

Met Dispater for the 2nd or 3rd time ever.  He's a tough one.

My main strategy at the end was to use conflict and run away from
battles.  It worked very well in the endgame.

The only time I got close to death was against Master Kaen.  Otherwise
I had bottles of full healing at the ready, but never used em.  I had
two amulets of life saving but never died.  I was never swallowed by an
air elemental in the plains.

I think for the ultimate game, besides pacifist which is just absurd,
is no polypile & no conflict in addition to all of the above.

I now feel I'm ready for Slash 'em.  Here goes nothing.

